Chapter 1

1.1 Introduction

This project focuses on the design and development of a Tic-Tac-Toe game using the Java programming language.
The application is intended to provide users with an interactive and user-friendly gaming experience through a graphical user interface(GUI).
The game will allow users to play against another person or compete against a computer-controlled opponent.

The project aims to develop practical programming skills through the application of Java programming concepts.
These include constuctors, access modifiers, control statements, graphical user interfaces and object-oriented programming principles.

The application will also include additional features such as score tracking, different AI difficulty levels, larger grid options and customisable game tokens.
Through this project, the group aims to demonstrate the software development process, from planning and design to implementation and testing.

